  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have serious doubts that even with the promises of QoL changes that will be implemented from mods; the process will be awfully slow and all requested features wont be able to make it in. \nThe man power of the dev team will never out pace the power of the collective modding community. There will just be too much out there to a single team to handle. So I suggest official lines for mod creators to get their mods mods check and filtered to something the dev team can feel safe having it run with their game. A process where the devs can monitor and control what get's added and when these mods get updated.\nOf course this will take resources to maintain but I assume the team has got a least the money to start support of such a program.",
